PQC migration (whitepaper 2.2.1): the foundational wrap primitive that
M5/M6/M7 layer on top of. wrapSecret(plaintext, keyId, key) returns a
WrappedSecret carrying a fresh 12-byte IV and a 16-byte AES-256-GCM
auth tag, sealed under the supplied keyId. The envelope survives any
downstream BLOB-vs-utf8 ambiguity because serializeWrappedSecret /
deserializeWrappedSecret round-trip through base64url-encoded JSON.

- src/security/secret-wrapping.ts: new file. Implements wrapSecret,
  unwrapSecret, serializeWrappedSecret, deserializeWrappedSecret, plus
  the WrappingKeyProvider interface that M5 (device-identity-store) and
  M6 (File/Env/Composite keyrings) plug into. Defensive shape checks at
  every boundary: 32-byte key, 12-byte IV, 16-byte auth tag, keyId
  presence + ≤128 chars, plaintext ≤64 KiB.
- src/security/secret-wrapping.test.ts: 25 invariants — round-trip across
  empty / 1952 / 4032 / 64 KiB plaintexts, IV uniqueness over 32 calls,
  tamper detection on ciphertext/IV/authTag, wrong-size key under same
  keyId, dropped/over-long keyId rejection, non-Buffer rejection, cap
  enforcement, serialize/deserialize round-trip + 4 malformed-input
  rejections, SecretWrappingError type contract.

